  LOC  OBJECT CODE    ADDR1 ADDR2  STMT   SOURCE STATEMENT                                       ASM 0201 07.10 09/27/26

                                      1 *---------------------------------------------------------------------*
                                      2 * XATEST  -  ASSEMBLE ONE OF EACH MACRO AND CHECK THE BYTES           *
                                      3 *                                                                     *
                                      4 * THIS IS NOT MEANT TO RUN.  IT EXISTS SO THE ASSEMBLER LISTING CAN BE*
                                      5 * COMPARED AGAINST KNOWN-GOOD ENCODINGS BEFORE ANY OF THESE MACROS IS *
                                      6 * TRUSTED IN REAL CODE.  FIVE OF THE ENCODINGS BELOW HAVE ALREADY BEEN*
                                      7 * EXECUTED SUCCESSFULLY UNDER HERCULES; THE REST COME FROM READING    *
                                      8 * SOURCE, WHICH IS WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.                              *
                                      9 *                                                                     *
                                     10 *   GLOBAL MACLIB XALIB                                               *
                                     11 *   ASSEMBLE XATEST (PRINT                                            *
                                     12 *                                                                     *
                                     13 * THEN READ XATEST LISTING AND COMPARE THE OBJECT COLUMN WITH THE     *
                                     14 * EXPECTED VALUES IN THE COMMENTS.  THE BASE AND DISPLACEMENT HALFWORD*
                                     15 * WILL DEPEND ON WHERE THE OPERANDS LAND, SO ONLY THE FIRST TWO BYTES *
                                     16 * ARE FIXED -- BUT THOSE ARE THE ONES THAT DECIDE WHICH INSTRUCTION   *
                                     17 * THE MACHINE EXECUTES.                                               *
                                     18 *---------------------------------------------------------------------*
                                     19 *
                                     20 * PRINT GEN,DATA IS NOT COSMETIC.  WITH NOGEN THE MACRO-GENERATED DC
                                     21 * STATEMENTS DO NOT APPEAR IN THE LISTING AT ALL, SO THE OBJECT BYTES
                                     22 * THIS TEST EXISTS TO READ WOULD BE INVISIBLE.  DATA SHOWS EVERY BYTE
                                     23 * OF A CONSTANT RATHER THAN THE FIRST EIGHT.
                                     24 *
                                     25          PRINT GEN,DATA
000000                               26 XATEST   CSECT
                                     27 *
                                     28 * REGISTER EQUATES FIRST.  ASSEMBLER F WANTS THE SYMBOLS IN A USING
                                     29 * STATEMENT ALREADY DEFINED, AND A FORWARD REFERENCE THERE WOULD FAIL
                                     30 * FOR A REASON THAT HAS NOTHING TO DO WITH THE MACROS UNDER TEST.
                                     31 *
                            00000    32 R0       EQU   0
                            00001    33 R1       EQU   1
                            00002    34 R2       EQU   2
                            00003    35 R3       EQU   3
                            00004    36 R4       EQU   4
                            0000E    37 R14      EQU   14
                            0000F    38 R15      EQU   15
                                     39 *
000000 05F0                          40          BALR  R15,0
                            00002    41          USING *,R15
                                     42 *
                                     43 * R1 MUST HOLD X'0001' IN THE HIGH HALFWORD AND THE SUBCHANNEL NUMBER
                                     44 * IN THE LOW BEFORE ANY OF THE SUBCHANNEL INSTRUCTIONS.  BITS 0-15
                                     45 * MUST BE EXACTLY 0001, NOT MERELY NON-ZERO.
                                     46 *
000002 5810 F046      00048          47          L     R1,SSIDW
                                     48 *
                                     49 *        EXPECT                     INSTRUCTION
                                     50 *        ------                     -----------
                                     51          STSCH SCHIB           *    B234  proven by execution
000006                               52+         DS    0H
000006 B234F0B6                      53+         DC    X'B234',S(SCHIB)
                                     54          MSCH  SCHIB           *    B232  proven by execution
00000A                               55+         DS    0H
                                                                                                               PAGE    3

